T}
.TE
.PP
If hook registration fails (e.g., the hook table is full), the hooks are
not registered and the level remains unchanged.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]level\f[R] \(em Desired observability level.
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]0\f[R] (\f[CR]OBSERVE_LEVEL_OFF\f[R]): Disable command event
hooks.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]1\f[R] (\f[CR]OBSERVE_LEVEL_COMMAND\f[R]): Enable pre/post command
events.
.IP \(bu 2
Values < 0 are clamped to 0.
.IP \(bu 2
Values > \f[CR]OBSERVE_LEVEL_MAX\f[R] are clamped to
\f[CR]OBSERVE_LEVEL_MAX\f[R].
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the level actually set after clamping.
This is always in the range [0, \f[CR]OBSERVE_LEVEL_MAX\f[R]].
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]observe_init\f[R](3), \f[CR]observe_cleanup\f[R](3)
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Can be called at any time during a session, not just during
initialization.
The v2 session handler calls this when the client sends an
\f[CR]observe\f[R] control message to change the level dynamically.
.IP \(bu 2
Hook registration is idempotent; calling with the same level that is
already active is a no\-op.
